{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon","id":608310,"title":"Best Favored Form for a Rahu Blood Talon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-30T12:22:55-07:00","id":608310,"title":"Best Favored Form for a Rahu Blood Talon","content":"I'm playing a Blood Talon Rahu (yay stereotypes) and I'm pretty much trying to become Death, Destroyer of worlds. I've never played a Rahu or a Blood Talon, but basically I want to be able to beat any werewolf in a brawl.<br /> <br /> I ask this because there are various merits (Favored Form, Fortified Form, Living Weapon) that apply to a specific form and none else. It's highly unlikely I'll have enough experience to bolster all my forms (and with favored form you can only ever choose one), so what's the best form to bolster with the idea that I will often be facing other werewolves?<br /> <br /> <br /> I am leaning toward Urshul for various reasons. My fighting style is the Relentless Assault style, which can be used in any form. Meaning that the primary advantage of the Dalu form is less important. I can only hold Garou form for 4 turns currently so it seems like a waste to put all that experience into a form I can only hold for a few seconds at a time.<br /> <br /> But at the same time, I expect I'll be fighting Werewolves in Garou form often enough that Garou is the only real response. Even if I add all the extra stats and armor to Urshul I am either making my Garou form obsolete/myself less likely to use it orrrr I'm just being suboptimal for fighting other Garou.<br /> <br /> The benefits of Garou (all day regen and screw your defense) are sort of more valuable than anything I can do to my Urshul form, but putting all that experience into a form that lasts so short seems unwise. What do y'all think.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also any further suggestions to help reach my character goals would be great. I currently have Slaughterer and Primal Strength as my facets, and my merits are basically just relentless assault and the Demolisher merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6422,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6422-lionel","user":"Lionel","date":". 07-30-2015, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6422-lionel","name":"Lionel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T13:02:12-07:00","id":608372,"title":"","content":"If you want the best warrior, then Gauru is, hands down, the best for outright brawls in my opinion. The form actually lasts all scene, if you're willing to fall into Wasu-Im, which, with the new rules, won't hurt your pack. So, its actually a lot better to rely on now than before. Especially when you look at some of the best gifts for your character (Strength/Rage) get better when you're in Wasu-Im. Absolutely worth thinking about.<br /> <br /> Each of the five forms has a role to play - Hishu is urban camo, Dalu is for urban hunts, dealing with large groups of humans and the like, Gauru is the war form, Urshul is more of a support unit, weakening the prey so that it can be finished off by Gauru, and Urhan is for long distance running and tracking. So, if you want to be a Destroyer, then you want Gauru, no question about it. <br /> <br /> Since you seem to be planning on investing in Favored Form, it seems that you'll have to be investing in Primal Urge as well (its a prereq), which will also increase your non-Death Rage Gauru form.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T13:21:11-07:00","id":608384,"title":"","content":"Urshul will only be a best option if for any reason you want to be on that form all-day long.<br /> <br /> And even without Wasu-Im, 4 turns will be enough for most fights with all the build for combat and help of your pack mates.<br /> <br /> Gauru is the only true way to become &quot;Death, Destroyer of Worlds&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T13:24:42-07:00","id":608387,"title":"","content":"Good points, guys. Well then question. Is Fortified Form a waste on Garou?<br /> <br /> My reasoning was that if I'm dueling another werewolf then they'll be in Garou form and then we're basically cancelling each other out for a while. And basically who wins that fight is really either who can last in Garou longest or who can prolong going into Garou longest, hence the reasoning for making an Urshul that can at least withstand a Garou's onslaught for some time.<br /> <br /> Edit: With increased Stamina, Primal Urge and Honor (for the rage facet) I can get Garou to last a fair amount of time, but it'll still come down to outlasting other werewolves. Especially if I'm fighting multiple werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6422,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6422-lionel","user":"Lionel","date":". 07-30-2015, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6422-lionel","name":"Lionel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T14:19:59-07:00","id":608428,"title":"","content":"Re: Fortified form @ Gauru: Not a waste in the case the opponent can do aggravated damage to you. And every werewolf can do so if they're willing to eat you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T14:26:53-07:00","id":608435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=608387#post608387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good points, guys. Well then question. Is Fortified Form a waste on Garou?<br /> <br /> My reasoning was that if I'm dueling another werewolf then they'll be in Garou form and then we're basically cancelling each other out for a while. And basically who wins that fight is really either who can last in Garou longest or who can prolong going into Garou longest, hence the reasoning for making an Urshul that can at least withstand a Garou's onslaught for some time.<br /> <br /> Edit: With increased Stamina, Primal Urge and Honor (for the rage facet) I can get Garou to last a fair amount of time, but it'll still come down to outlasting other werewolves. Especially if I'm fighting multiple werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly why you want Gauru as your favored form. A fight between two werewolves will almost always come down to who can maintain Gauru the longest. Having more stamina in Gauru form will let you maintain the form for longer, which gives you a huge advantage over any Uratha opponent who isn't willing to Death Rage just to beat you. And against those who are, having enhanced natural weaponry and/or natural armor will give you the edge you need in a Kuruth vs. Kuruth battle. Hands down, Gauru form is the best tool for fighting other werewolves, so if that's what you want your character to be good at, that's the form you want to buff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T14:38:07-07:00","id":608444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=608435#post608435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having more stamina in Gauru form will let you maintain the form for longer</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. The duration is measured off of your Hishu Stamina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T16:09:05-07:00","id":608555,"title":"","content":"Honestly I never thought that made much sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T17:45:47-07:00","id":608670,"title":"","content":"Yeah come to think of it, Fortified Form makes a lot of sense for resisting aggravated damage, but also for taking on multiple enemies who might be trying to fill your health levels from lethal into aggravated. So does the Glory facet from rage. The goal is to make it so that they can't bypass your health in lethal, and anything that makes that even more difficult is great.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T22:46:56-07:00","id":608984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=608444#post608444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. The duration is measured off of your Hishu Stamina.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, my mistake. Still, it's usually going to come down to a Gauru vs. Gauru fight, and extra Stamina and Fortified Form will help make it harder for them to wrap damage around to agg, while Living Weapon will help get around their armor if they have it and deal more health levels of damage to make wrapping around on them easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T06:00:34-07:00","id":609297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=608435#post608435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And against those who are, having enhanced natural weaponry and/or natural armor will give you the edge you need in a Kuruth vs. Kuruth battle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that you won't be fighting a Kuruth vs. Kuruth battle; Death Raging Uratha treat other Death Raging Uratha as friendlies and don't attack them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T06:17:06-07:00","id":609310,"title":"","content":"Huh. I though that only applied to packmates. Does it not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T07:04:04-07:00","id":609357,"title":"","content":"Nope. Everyone is a target under <i>Basu-Im</i> except for other werewolves in the same stage of Death Rage, regardless of pack affiliations.<br /> <br /> Mass Death Rage causes the resulting ball of death to explode <i>outwards</i> rather than turning inwards.<br /> <br /> Edit: Notably this does mean Gauru upgrades can be a double-edged sword when you start chewing on your own packmates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T07:05:49-07:00","id":609360,"title":"","content":"Nope. All your pack mates are lured into falling into Kuruth when you do, so chances are you'll be a pack of Death Raging wolves. But the book doesn't specify that only death raging packmates are immune. So, yes, a Forsaken and Pure can both death rage together and never fight, despite being enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T07:18:36-07:00","id":609367,"title":"","content":"Just to note, this isn't a mistake either - it was an explicit design decision we took.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T08:59:39-07:00","id":609531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=609367#post609367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to note, this isn't a mistake either - it was an explicit design decision we took.</div> </div> </div> </div>What were the design considerations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T09:46:30-07:00","id":609615,"title":"","content":"Probably avoid the chronicle coming to early terms with a fight to death between frenzied Urathas, and make the Death Rage into a concern, not a weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:01:41-07:00","id":609753,"title":"","content":"Not a fan of that particular decision, doesn't make sense to me that you would just stop attacking the thing you want to kill so badly you went into a berserk rage rather than focusing on killing that thing to the exclusion of everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:08:50-07:00","id":609769,"title":"","content":"I think Kuruth taps into some primordial part of them. The People Do Not Murder The People. Father Wolf's bane. Werewolves weren't meant to be divided by factions and killing each other. That's something time and change has made occasionally necessary, but the soul of the predator remains the same.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I prefer urshul for it. I like the speed and strength. I recognize that gauru is mechanically better, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:17:37-07:00","id":609777,"title":"","content":"I'd consider the werewolf's last conscious thought to drive their behaviour somewhat, if appropriate. I.E. If you were fighting another werewolf and both death raged you'd consider all werewolves in kuruth friendly <i>except that one</i>.<br /> <br /> Failing that, relentless assault. I figure it works in death rage for a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:22:37-07:00","id":609783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=609360#post609360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. All your pack mates are lured into falling into Kuruth when you do, so chances are you'll be a pack of Death Raging wolves. But the book doesn't specify that only death raging packmates are immune. So, yes, a Forsaken and Pure can both death rage together and never fight, despite being enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's going to make some awkward morning after conversations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:24:47-07:00","id":609785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=609783#post609783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's going to make some awkward morning after conversations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you cage yourself up in your cellar before you rage, Kuruth should always lead to awkward moments after waking up. And even then, you might wake up outside your cage.<br /> <br /> For instance, in my last game, my character was in a locked room with a person with two guns with silver bullets. When he awoke from Kuruth, he could only find one of the guns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-31-2015, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:36:32-07:00","id":609788,"title":"","content":"So nobody but Nofather sees any merit in choosing Urshul as the form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6422-lionel","name":"Lionel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:05:20-07:00","id":609809,"title":"","content":"There's definitely merit in favoring Urshul, it's just not the optimal form for fighting other werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:41:32-07:00","id":609839,"title":"","content":"I favored <i><b>Urshul </b></i>for my <i><b>Cahalith Hunter In Darkness </b></i>in 1st Edition. Best form ever for straight out fighting, in my opinion. If I wanted to Murder something, then I took <i><b>Primal Form... </b></i>Used Garou only a couple of times, and Primal Form only a few more than that. Urshul was my go to form for combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T13:26:04-07:00","id":609868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=609839#post609839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I favored <i><b>Urshul </b></i>for my <i><b>Cahalith Hunter In Darkness </b></i>in 1st Edition. Best form ever for straight out fighting, in my opinion. If I wanted to Murder something, then I took <i><b>Primal Form... </b></i>Used Garou only a couple of times, and Primal Form only a few more than that. Urshul was my go to form for combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here, though in 1st Edition Garou was a lot less effective as a war form than it is now. Primal Fear and the Regeneration are both so amazing that it's clearly and undeniably the war form now. The matter for me though is the temporary nature of it. If I'm fighting a whole pack of Uratha (not on my own, but still) the battle is going to last more than 4 turns, and I feel like I should be more concerned with what happens after my Garou limit runs out and I still have to fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6422-lionel","name":"Lionel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T13:46:29-07:00","id":609898,"title":"","content":"That's an important point to think about. One of the benefits of urshul is it can run far and fast. Theoretically you could, when an enemy rages, run away while it's distracted with something else, then come in for the kill when their rage is worn out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T14:04:24-07:00","id":609921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon#post608310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty much trying to become Death, Destroyer of worlds... basically I want to be able to beat any werewolf in a brawl.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why no one is talking about Urshul.<br /> <br /> Back on 1st ed you could argue for Urshul. I used it and fared well even being a Strength 1 Ithaeur. And even now you surely can point out benefits on Urshul and wish to invest in it.<br /> <br /> In the end, though, Gauru is much more deadly now. The forms have clear advantages to execute their functions, and Gauru simply does the job.<br /> <br /> He wants to be a rounded combatant with some tricks under the sleeve? I would advise Urshul. He wants to &quot;beat any werewolf in a brawl&quot;? Gauru is the only sensible option.<br /> <br /> Oh, and again, don't look at it as a 4 turns limit. Work WITH Basu-Im in mind, not against it at all costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T14:33:51-07:00","id":609964,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. Though because of the fact that Basu Im doesn't target other werewolves in Death Rage, I feel like it's sort of a nonfactor for my purposes. Though I do like the idea of being unstoppable in death rage. Thanks for all the input, guys. I think I agree for the most part. Still a little hesitant, but the points definitely make too much sense to ignore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6422-lionel","name":"Lionel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T17:32:28-07:00","id":610185,"title":"","content":"Basu Im only doesn't target your own pack members in Kuruth. You can target enemy packs just fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T17:59:26-07:00","id":610206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=610185#post610185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basu Im only doesn't target your own pack members in Kuruth. You can target enemy packs just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The book says any wolves in Basu-Im. 'When in Basu-Im, a werewolf suffers rage as though in Gauru, but everyone is a victim except other werewolves in Basu-Im.'<br /> <br /> Only other packmates are inspired to go into rage when you go into rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-31-2015, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T03:18:31-07:00","id":610622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=609868#post609868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I should be more concerned with what happens after my Garou limit runs out and I still have to fight.</div> </div> </div> </div> invest in Strength and Rage Gifts. Perfected rage adds Honor dots to your Gauru duration. Purity in both adds to Strength. Berserker's Might reduces damage. <br /> The Father's Form lets you run in Gauru form without time limit until you suffer Purity dots in damage or make an attack. Favored Form Requires raising PU (and you'll want Advanced Action on brawl attacks), which also raises your Stamina by 1, most likely <br /> <br /> Lots of ways to make Gauru last longer, and you'll be wanting to invest in things that apply equally inside and outside Gauru as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-01-2015, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T04:08:50-07:00","id":610649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=610185#post610185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basu Im only doesn't target your own pack members in Kuruth. You can target enemy packs just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>That directly contradicts what Chris said back on page 1 of this thread. That's the way it'll work in my games, but that isn't how it's presented in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T04:30:54-07:00","id":610654,"title":"","content":"Yes, I know, and I note Chris says it was an explicit design decision. I don't recall that conversation (and haven't found it in my archive). It's not how I recalled the design working, but I stand corrected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T11:39:04-07:00","id":611108,"title":"","content":"I like your way better if that makes any difference. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T12:37:44-07:00","id":611209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=609531#post609531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What were the design considerations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Several, but two significant ones very roughly summarised:<br /> <br /> 1) The Endless Furball of Violence - When multiple Uratha entered Death Rage from opposing sides under rules where rager attacked rager, they would then end up in a fight where the constant Gauru regeneration would likely be more than any of them could inflict on their opponent. Combat optimised Uratha might do it but, with raging essentially denying the player the ability to make intelligent use of their capabilities, you ended up with fundamentally boring fights between raging werewolves while everyone waits for the <i>Basu-Im</i> to cease. Who wants to play out 200 combat rounds of Uratha punching each other in the face over and over just in case someone manages to get an edge? This feeds into the second point...<br /> <br /> 2) Death Rage Is Bad - Death Rage is <i>not</i> a go-to fight winner. Doing it to overcome a foe is and should be a massive risk with likely serious consequences. The targeting rules for <i>Basu-Im</i> ensure that the horror remains - you don't get to just flip into it and go 'oh well, it's fine, I'll just be killing the other guys and leaving my pack alone.' When Death Rage spreads, all that werewolf violence goes <i>outwards</i>, not conveniently remains targeted on the people you specifically want dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T13:54:07-07:00","id":611288,"title":"","content":"Hmm... 1 makes a lot of sense to me. 2 seems like it would be a reason to <i>allow</i> you to target other Death Raging werewolves, or at least a reason to not make Kuruth infectious, since in most fights the only other Death Raging werewolves will be your packmates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T14:18:20-07:00","id":611331,"title":"","content":"Kuruth <i>is </i>a weapon. Just not one you set off in an area with anyone you don't want to kill in it. It's a bomb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T16:54:17-07:00","id":611463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=611288#post611288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... 1 makes a lot of sense to me. 2 seems like it would be a reason to <i>allow</i> you to target other Death Raging werewolves, or at least a reason to not make Kuruth infectious, since in most fights the only other Death Raging werewolves will be your packmates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without 2, on the other side of the table you have the routinely larger Pure packs also death raging and targeting Forsaken players and rushing after them for however long their Kuruth lasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T18:13:42-07:00","id":611516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=611463#post611463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Without 2, on the other side of the table you have the routinely larger Pure packs also death raging and targeting Forsaken players and rushing after them for however long their Kuruth lasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does sound like something the Pure would do. Is that a problem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T18:17:21-07:00","id":611518,"title":"","content":"It makes pretty much any fight with the Pure a near-guaranteed loss that happens off screen without any player agency.<br /> <br /> Yes, I have a problem with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-01-2015, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T20:01:30-07:00","id":611709,"title":"","content":"To me, reason #2 is pretty good. It does deliver more horror to the setting and makes Kuruth something to not be used lightly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T20:05:49-07:00","id":611712,"title":"","content":"I'm confused. Being unable to attack Death Raging werewolves, and your packmates catching your Death Rage makes it <i>less</i> safe to use around your pack mates? How?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T20:09:55-07:00","id":611715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=611518#post611518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes pretty much any fight with the Pure a near-guaranteed loss that happens off screen without any player agency.<br /> <br /> Yes, I have a problem with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh... I don't see that. Either the Forsaken and the Pure can both use Death Rage against each other, or neither of them can. Either way, they have access to the same tools, only the Pure have greater numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T20:27:33-07:00","id":611760,"title":"","content":"Yeah but the lack of player agency thing would be boring. It sounds like an exciting and terrifying scenario, two werewolves fighting in death rage, but it really just makes it so that all fights would end with Death Rage with very little consequence. Sort of cheapens the effect. Players relying on it to turn it up to 11 pretty much anytime things get serious would also just lead to hour long forever healing battles which end up equating to the dreaded slap fight which sounds cool, but in practice would just be kind of lame.<br /> <br /> At least that's how I feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T23:08:23-07:00","id":611915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=611760#post611760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but the lack of player agency thing would be boring. It sounds like an exciting and terrifying scenario, two werewolves fighting in death rage, but it really just makes it so that all fights would end with Death Rage with very little consequence. Sort of cheapens the effect. Players relying on it to turn it up to 11 pretty much anytime things get serious would also just lead to hour long forever healing battles which end up equating to the dreaded slap fight which sounds cool, but in practice would just be kind of lame.<br /> <br /> At least that's how I feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was point 1 and I fully agree with it. Point 2 seems extremely counter-intuitive to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T23:23:22-07:00","id":611926,"title":"","content":"Well, no, it was both points. There would otherwise be no real incentive not to go death rage, and it's supposed to be a scary thing to embrace. If my pack was fighting a pack of Pure, we'd basically just want to go death rage as soon as possible. There would literally be no reason not to, and Garou would essentially be unnecessary. Garou is the war form, it's the form you want to use for war. The function of Kuruth shouldn't be &quot;The War Form but longer&quot;, it's a terrifying loss of control of agency. So it makes sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T01:03:05-07:00","id":611957,"title":"","content":"I disagree. The purpose of Gauru is to close in and make the kill after the prey is weakened - you get the job done and regeneration protects you so you're not damaged for the next hunt. (There's good reason for predators ambushing, striking fast, or harrying their prey before moving in for the kill. Struggling or desperate prey can injure the predator, reducing its effectiveness and possibly leading to its death.)<br /> <br /> Werewolf vs werewolf (hunting) is more complicated (assuming things are equal between packs). Your tactic is to do everything you can to wear the prey down and force it to take Gauru first, limiting its options for later, and ensuring you can maintain Gauru after it has exhausted its reserve. You keep pinging at it, knowing that it can withstand the damage but also knowing it's running on a clock.<br /> <br /> Under my original understanding of Basu-Im targets, if the prey runs into Kuruth, you take Gauru and go toe-to-toe for as long as possible, as it tears chunks of you and you hold off Kuruth of your own just that little bit longer, knowing that you'll win the fight when it collapses into Hishu before you and you destroy it. The biggest risk of both of you being in Kuruth is that you'll probably start chewing down chunks of each other for the Aggravated damage, and when one is dead you'll rampage against everything else until your time is up. IMO, this scenario is like a tactical nuclear strike - it will almost certainly cause collateral damage to innocents, but you can at least target it. Exciting, and means the Blood Talons have to work hard to become masters of choosing the right moment, chasing down the most dangerous foes, putting their lives on the line to tip the prey over the edge first, and taking responsibility for the impossible cost/benefit analysis of how many innocent deaths this werewolf is worth.<br /> <br /> Under the official version, Kuruth isn't a nuclear option. It's almost pointless. Nuclear weapons are constructed as deterrents to prevent escalation, but if a country gets desperate enough and pushed far enough, they'll deploy the nuke knowing that they enemy will be dead, but so will untold numbers of innocents, and likely themselves when the enemy counter strikes. In this version, Kuruth is the (near) guarantee you'll walk away, and so will your enemy. There will still be collateral damage, but not to the actual prey. You launch your nuke, they launch their nuke, you come back next week and do it again. In this scenario, the most effective hunting tactic for Blood Talons is to arm all their Wolf-Blooded and humans with silver - don't bother with timing or tactics, just draw them into a fight and hit them with silver. If they go Kuruth, run away while firing silver. There's not much point doing anything else. You can't gain advantage by harrying them or forcing them to a poor choice first. You want the aggravated option first time, every time. No Blood Talon should ever travel without her gang of tooled-up, silver bearing humans.<br /> <br /> <i>Edit:</i><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=611926#post611926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou is the war form, it's the form you want to use for war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gauru is the <i>killing </i>form, not the war form. War form is from 1st edition, and 1st ed Gauru was really poor at being used for war. We specifically went out of our way to ensure 2nd ed Gauru had purpose in the hunt, and that purpose is killing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 08-02-2015, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T05:18:21-07:00","id":612061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=611712#post611712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused. Being unable to attack Death Raging werewolves, and your packmates catching your Death Rage makes it <i>less</i> safe to use around your pack mates? How?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, never said that. The horror is in that <u>play with monsters</u> part. If you don't attack other werewolves in Kuruth, what happens is that either they hold their ground without Death Rage against the ones who entered it, or the werewolves involved spread after other targets without any control. That's far more interesting than using Kuruth to finish all your fights without really thinking about them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your tactic is to do everything you can to wear the prey down and force it to take Gauru first, limiting its options for later, and ensuring you can maintain Gauru after it has exhausted its reserve.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with your reasoning is that Primal Urge changes drastically the duration of Kuruth, so no, it wouldn't be a tactical nuke. Since even 1 minute means 20 turns, either the combat would be resolved by random chance during Kuruth because someone manages to cause enough lethal to go aggravated, or the greater Primal Urge wins, always. Only between PU 1 and 2 there are no difference in Basu-Im duration.<br /> <br /> Your idea does have its merit, but it ultimately doesn't work that way. All it would do is to guarantee victory to higher PU, what's kinda boring.<br /> <br /> And a gang of silver-armed goons where STILL be a better tactic, by the way, if viable at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T06:11:24-07:00","id":612141,"title":"","content":"A gang of silver-armed goons is still a good anti-werewolf tactic. Under current Kuruth, it's still one of the only viable tactics, as few Uratha will let themselves be killed by less than aggravated damage without going to Gauru to try and avoid it, and then Kuruth if all seems lost; you might as well hit them with damage they can't instantly heal before they lose themselves to the rage.<br /> <br /> Under RAW, the highest PU is still likely to win - unless your (non-Uratha) pack somehow manages to channel you off on your own, or the Storyteller gives contrived reasons for the multiple Gauru to split up, you all rage together until the weakest PU falls over, then the others kill him as he's (technically) no longer protected. the protection against this is to try and stay close enough to watch for your packmate to drop, but distant enough that they don't target you. When they drop, attack the remainder so they focus on the threat and not the fresh meat.<br /> <br /> The Totem's Wrath facet of the Gift of Pack is a good bet when facing a Death Raged Uratha - it gives your side a rampaging Gauru who doesn't recognise another pack's immunity and can happily gulp down werewolf flesh until the enemy is no more or it runs out of Essence (which can take some time while it's chowing down on chunks of werewolf).<br /> <br /> Edit: I forgot to add, this difficulty is part of what makes Blood Talons awesome, and their sacred prey most dangerous. Harry the prey, hit and run. Push him to get angrier, keep at it until he's worn out and goes Gauru. Keep control, keep hitting, push him to his limit. Then out of desperation he goes Kuruth. You'd better have done your homework as well, and worked out his likely PU. <br /> <br /> &quot;Sir, he's going Kuruth.&quot;<br /> &quot;Start the clock. We've got to keep him distracted for 10 minutes, then he's ours. Let's try and keep him contained, no need to destroy everything just yet.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 08-02-2015, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T07:54:35-07:00","id":612220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=611926#post611926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no, it was both points. There would otherwise be no real incentive not to go death rage, and it's supposed to be a scary thing to embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm saying is, the rules as written don't make it a scary thing to embrace, because when you Death Rage, your pack Death Rages, and you can't attack your pack members when they are in Death Rage. That means you never have to worry about accidentally killing your packmates with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=611926#post611926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my pack was fighting a pack of Pure, we'd basically just want to go death rage as soon as possible. There would literally be no reason not to, and Garou would essentially be unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>As it stands, there is no reason <i>to</i> use it, because if they also Death Rage, you can't attack each other. which I understand, because it would be a very long and pretty boring fight if you could. But, If you could attack other Death Raging werewolves with it, there would be a very good reason not to: you don't want to hurt your own packmates accidently. The inability to attack other Death Raging werewolves makes Kuruth <i>much safer</i> to use, since it's infectious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=611926#post611926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou is the war form, it's the form you want to use for war. The function of Kuruth shouldn't be &quot;The War Form but longer&quot;, it's a terrifying loss of control of agency. So it makes sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Gauru is actually the Killing Form now. Its purpose is supposed to be dealing the final blow, not going to war. Kuruth is supposed to be a terrifying loss of control and agency, and it kind of is, but currently you can rest assured you'll probably never kill any of your packmates while you're in Death Rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T08:46:07-07:00","id":612273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=612220#post612220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm saying is, the rules as written don't make it a scary thing to embrace, because when you Death Rage, your pack Death Rages, and you can't attack your pack members when they are in Death Rage. That means you never have to worry about accidentally killing your packmates with it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, not your whole pack. Lets not forget that we have wolf-blooded and humans in the pack as well as werewolves. So, that means that, in an Forsaken-Pure battle, and all the wolves Death Rage, the blooded and mortals suffer. Pure would generally be cool with that - are the Forsaken?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T09:01:42-07:00","id":612300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=612273#post612273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, not your whole pack. Lets not forget that we have wolf-blooded and humans in the pack as well as werewolves. So, that means that, in an Forsaken-Pure battle, and all the wolves Death Rage, the blooded and mortals suffer. Pure would generally be cool with that - are the Forsaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but they aren't usually part of the hunting party, so if human and wolf-blooded packmates are involved in the fight, things are pretty FUBAR'd to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T09:02:19-07:00","id":612302,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but if you attacked other packmates in Death Rage TPKs would just be a thing that happened often. As the Rahu in my group with Predator's Unmatched Pursuit and a whole host of other facets that enhance Death Rage, I know for a fact that I would kill my whole group in Death Rage, whether they matched me form for form or not. Literally they could not escape me or take me down barring Storyteller intervention. Which is cool and terrifying, I certainly don't disagree, but also might be a little too dangerous.<br /> <br /> I do agree with the point that it would be scarier if you attacked your packmates, but you do when they aren't in Kuruth, so that's covered - join me or die means that Wolfblooded and Human packmates are always in danger, and so are werewolves who want to stop you from killing them (because they have to resist Kuruth to do that).<br /> <br /> As far as narrative reason that uratha in Kuruth don't attack each other, that is a bit less solid for me. I guess they're all one big pack on one big hunt? I mean, narrativewise for me it would make sense to attack the Pure in Kuruth. So that's the only part that doesn't quite hold for me, and I wish it was addressed in the book. But I can look past that.<br /> <br /> And yeah, sorry for the &quot;war form&quot; hold over. Though I'd still think it probably is the <i>war</i> form, I understand the reason for the shift in terminology. If Kuruth attacked Kuruth, it would probably be the war form.<br /> <br /> And to specifically Bunyip, I do see your point about the nuclear option and it's cool to see it that way, but my worry is that it wouldn't play out in most cases. Kuruth would become a necessary component of every uratha v uratha struggle, not what happens when they lose control or strain themselves in desperation. More like two people in a fist fight with their guns holstered. As opposed to two people in a fist fight with a monster inside that just wants to tear the world apart.<br /> <br /> Okay maybe that analogy isn't perfect. And I do see your point, and I think either makes some sense to use mechanically, but I err on the side of not Death Raging everytime we fight the Pure because it means that leaves a much higher chance that I will just die anytime I fight a werewolf stronger than me and I won't even be in control of my character when it happens and while the image of two werewolves destroying everything in their path during an epic fight, it'll probably just end up being a slap fight forever until one dies, which is just not as interesting as you both leveling a whole small town because you lost control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 08-02-2015, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T09:04:32-07:00","id":612306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=612300#post612300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but they aren't usually part of the hunting party, so if human and wolf-blooded packmates are involved in the fight, things are pretty FUBAR'd to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, it seems that a good portion of them are part of hunting parties, from what I read. Maybe not for the standard Player Character group, since most of them will be full wolves and only hunting with the PCs. But that assumes that we're all playing full werewolves. Or someone didn't follow them. Or that the fight is happening some place where non-werewolves happen to be - who said the Pure were always the prey?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T09:45:33-07:00","id":612336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=612306#post612306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, it seems that a good portion of them are part of hunting parties, from what I read. Maybe not for the standard Player Character group, since most of them will be full wolves and only hunting with the PCs. But that assumes that we're all playing full werewolves. Or someone didn't follow them. Or that the fight is happening some place where non-werewolves happen to be - who said the Pure were always the prey?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... In my reading, the werewolves of the pack form the hunting party, while the wolf-blooded have other roles like maintaining the territory while the werewolves hunt. Occasionally Wolf-Blooded can be a part of the hunting party, but it is rare, which is why it constitutes a 3-dot Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T11:57:27-07:00","id":612475,"title":"","content":"The book doesn't define how much wolf-blooded take part on the hunt, so you can't have expectations. Also, against Pures you probably can find some wolf-blooded and mortals being throw in the fray anyway, because the don't care. But the Forsaken do, they ar still people, and probably victims.<br /> <br /> And no, you won't have this safe scenario. Again, the time of Basu-Im depends on PU. So your pack isn't safe from your Kuruth because they raged with you. If they hunt together during Rage, what will happen is that the highest PU in the pack will kill all the others.<br /> <br /> If they don't, well... NOW you're treating actual play as a White-Room when it isn't. Your raging werewolf won't stay in place carving stones with his claws. When all the werewolfs in scene are raging, there are no viable targets for all those Basu-Ims. So they will FIND targets. And the ST can shove you on any situation he desires. At minimum you have 10 minutes in Gauru form looking constantly for prey. Have fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T12:03:47-07:00","id":612480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=612220#post612220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The inability to attack other Death Raging werewolves makes Kuruth <i>much safer</i> to use, since it's infectious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Safe in the sense that you'll kill your non-werewolf packmates, the non-werewolf enemy pack members and also any non-werewolf innocent bystanders close enough for you to track down with your keen werewolf senses, but you and your werewolf packmates are not at much risk? I suppose that yes, it's somewhat safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T12:09:31-07:00","id":612485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=612220#post612220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm saying is, the rules as written don't make it a scary thing to embrace, because when you Death Rage, your pack Death Rages, and you can't attack your pack members when they are in Death Rage. That means you never have to worry about accidentally killing your packmates with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The scary thing is supposed to be you might wander off and kill someone walking their dog, the family of the dog-walker who came to see what all the screams were about, and the police they called when they discovered a bunch of freaky monsters who were about to kill them.<br /> <br /> That said, it's still possible to kill packmates, if you don't go into death rage when the others do or if you drop out first. But the focus seems to be more on, 'What have I done!?' than, 'Okay Danni, time to make a new character after that last Death Rage.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-02-2015, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T12:53:50-07:00","id":612516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=612475#post612475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book doesn't define how much wolf-blooded take part on the hunt, so you can't have expectations. Also, against Pures you probably can find some wolf-blooded and mortals being throw in the fray anyway, because the don't care. But the Forsaken do, they ar still people, and probably victims.<br /> <br /> And no, you won't have this safe scenario. Again, the time of Basu-Im depends on PU. So your pack isn't safe from your Kuruth because they raged with you. If they hunt together during Rage, what will happen is that the highest PU in the pack will kill all the others.<br /> <br /> If they don't, well... NOW you're treating actual play as a White-Room when it isn't. Your raging werewolf won't stay in place carving stones with his claws. When all the werewolfs in scene are raging, there are no viable targets for all those Basu-Ims. So they will FIND targets. And the ST can shove you on any situation he desires. At minimum you have 10 minutes in Gauru form looking constantly for prey. Have fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt the Uratha still in the throes of Kuruth will target the the early exhausted. They lay there, limp. No threat there, nothing running like prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T13:34:53-07:00","id":612563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=612485#post612485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The scary thing is supposed to be you might wander off and kill someone walking their dog, the family of the dog-walker who came to see what all the screams were about, and the police they called when they discovered a bunch of freaky monsters who were about to kill them.<br /> <br /> That said, it's still possible to kill packmates, if you don't go into death rage when the others do or if you drop out first. But the focus seems to be more on, 'What have I done!?' than, 'Okay Danni, time to make a new character after that last Death Rage.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's why Death Rage is dangerous. That's a risk whether or not you can target the pure you're fighting, so I don't understand why &quot;to make it more dangerous&quot; would be a reason to make you not able to target the pure you're fighting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T13:48:17-07:00","id":612573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=612563#post612563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a risk whether or not you can target the pure you're fighting, so I don't understand why &quot;to make it more dangerous&quot; would be a reason to make you not able to target the pure you're fighting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, one on one, there's little risk in going death rage against another Pure. Because they death rage, and you both cancel each other out fighting each other in death rage until someone passes out first and dies.<br /> <br /> And in more realistic encounters, the Forsaken pack fights against the Pure pack and the Pure pack has superior numbers so are more likely to destroy the Forsaken, who are unable to flee and are stuck fighting an opponent without being able to do anything other than fight that opponent.<br /> <br /> It's not about Death Rage being <i>dangerous</i>, it's about Death Rage being <i>bad</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=611209#post611209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">2) Death Rage Is Bad - Death Rage is <i>not</i> a go-to fight winner.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>You should survive it, and wonder whose blood you're covered in. When they awaken, your character should have brief flashes of memory, people screaming, trying to run away. Did they make it? It should be something you're afraid to do because you don't know what will happen when the predator is in control. It shouldn't be an, 'I win,' or, 'I make a new character' switch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T14:29:49-07:00","id":612604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=612573#post612573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because, one on one, there's little risk in going death rage against another Pure. Because they death rage, and you both cancel each other out fighting each other in death rage until someone passes out first and dies.<br /> <br /> And in more realistic encounters, the Forsaken pack fights against the Pure pack and the Pure pack has superior numbers so are more likely to destroy the Forsaken, who are unable to flee and are stuck fighting an opponent without being able to do anything other than fight that opponent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not seeing what that has to do with point 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=612573#post612573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about Death Rage being <i>dangerous</i>, it's about Death Rage being <i>bad</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> You should survive it, and wonder whose blood you're covered in. When they awaken, your character should have brief flashes of memory, people screaming, trying to run away. Did they make it? It should be something you're afraid to do because you don't know what will happen when the predator is in control. It shouldn't be an, 'I win,' or, 'I make a new character' switch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree. I don't see how being able to attack other Death-Raging werewolves makes this not the case though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T15:05:32-07:00","id":612632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=612604#post612604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I agree. I don't see how being able to attack other Death-Raging werewolves makes this not the case though.</div> </div> </div> </div>By definition a thing which does not immediately die is going to hold the attention of the berserker demigod for much longer than more fragile assets like teammates and passersby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T07:48:18-07:00","id":613360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=611209#post611209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Several, but two significant ones very roughly summarised:<br /> <br /> 1) The Endless Furball of Violence - When multiple Uratha entered Death Rage from opposing sides under rules where rager attacked rager, they would then end up in a fight where the constant Gauru regeneration would likely be more than any of them could inflict on their opponent. Combat optimised Uratha might do it but, with raging essentially denying the player the ability to make intelligent use of their capabilities, you ended up with fundamentally boring fights between raging werewolves while everyone waits for the <i>Basu-Im</i> to cease. Who wants to play out 200 combat rounds of Uratha punching each other in the face over and over just in case someone manages to get an edge? This feeds into the second point...<br /> <br /> 2) Death Rage Is Bad - Death Rage is <i>not</i> a go-to fight winner. Doing it to overcome a foe is and should be a massive risk with likely serious consequences. The targeting rules for <i>Basu-Im</i> ensure that the horror remains - you don't get to just flip into it and go 'oh well, it's fine, I'll just be killing the other guys and leaving my pack alone.' When Death Rage spreads, all that werewolf violence goes <i>outwards</i>, not conveniently remains targeted on the people you specifically want dead.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm.... number 2 would be more believable if a good number of Rage and Strength Gifts weren't all better when used in Basu-Im too. I was just looking over them, and saw how all those Gifts are without cost in Basu-Im. <br /> <br /> The problem with Death Rage is that, while its supposed to be bad, there are absolutely benefits for going into it. Yes, you will indiscriminately kill things. However, that relies on there being things to indiscriminately kill. Tracking the Azlu down to an abandoned factory in the middle of the night? We're looking at collateral damage and the potential to fall into a trap, but not exactly a lot of potential for killing innocents. Especially if we set up a boundary ward, or hunt in the Hisil. <br /> <br /> Its supposed to be bad and, yes, even dangerous. But is it actually playing out that way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T09:58:01-07:00","id":613564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=613360#post613360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with Death Rage is that, while its supposed to be bad, there are absolutely benefits for going into it. Yes, you will indiscriminately kill things. However, that relies on there being things to indiscriminately kill. Tracking the Azlu down to an abandoned factory in the middle of the night? We're looking at collateral damage and the potential to fall into a trap, but not exactly a lot of potential for killing innocents. Especially if we set up a boundary ward, or hunt in the Hisil.<br /> <br /> Its supposed to be bad and, yes, even dangerous. But is it actually playing out that way?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are benefits, but they're very risky. You're locking yourself into at least 10 minutes of combat. It's a last solution kind of thing, and in certain conditional cases, sure it cuts down the risks. But not every story is going to lead to a bunch of baddies in an abandoned factory. Everyone won't have their Wasu-Im trigger within running distance of an empty building no one else has a chance of walking into. Putting up a ward won't keep out the homeless who're already squatting there, or the wolf-blood children the shartha have held captive.<br /> <br /> But the empty building is still a possibility to throw at the players if a ST just wants them to clean out some minor foes without too much worry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T11:31:30-07:00","id":613723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=613564#post613564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the empty building is still a possibility to throw at the players if a ST just wants them to clean out some minor foes without too much worry.</div> </div> </div> </div> That was just one example. We could be in empty stretches of wilderness, inside the Hisil, set up a ward so that it drives away anyone who'd be a target... This isn't something the ST &quot;throws at&quot; the players. Its something that the players can be actively arranged for.<br /> <br /> As for the triggers? Just stay Gauru, go over the limit, and everyone has their trigger, right then and there. You can willingly fail rolls, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T11:58:18-07:00","id":613753,"title":"","content":"Elodoth are also pretty good for that. Heck, the Rahu writeup's Connection for Elodoth says &quot;wait until I get to the corner, then make me rage.&quot; So the idea of kuruth being used as a weapon is definitely supported by the book. It should be a weapon of last resort, but it's definitely a weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T12:06:39-07:00","id":613761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=613723#post613723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That was just one example. We could be in empty stretches of wilderness, inside the Hisil, set up a ward so that it drives away anyone who'd be a target... This isn't something the ST &quot;throws at&quot; the players. Its something that the players can be actively arranged for.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're running away to a safe place to hide death rage is doing its job of making death rage be a scary proposition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the triggers? Just stay Gauru, go over the limit, and everyone has their trigger, right then and there. You can willingly fail rolls, after all. </div> </div> </div>You can death rage all you want willingly, it won't stop the triggers from triggering. The point of them is that while you can prepare, you can't prepare for everything. A couple games ago my character got struck by silver bullets and jumped into Wasu-Im. She was defeated in the round after that, but the damage was done and my character was rushing towards death rage in the middle of a parking garage. Sure he ran to get away from a place where people might show up and cars would be notably destroyed but he ended up trailing blood down the garage and street. Some of the specific triggers are easier to avoid, like swallowing human blood, but there are also things like being targeted by a supernatural power or hearing a wolf howl when your auspice is in the sky, things that could be triggered in a movie theater or at home watching a movie or at a club.<br /> <br /> A storyteller can eliminate the risk. They can have empty buildings everywhere. They can have the hisil empty so you won't be mindlessly attacking spirits that were beginning to appreciate you, a barren wilderness without hunters or other supernaturals that's always within 3 seconds to 15 minutes worth of travel away from wherever you may be. But that's avoiding the story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=613753#post613753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elodoth are also pretty good for that. Heck, the Rahu writeup's Connection for Elodoth says &quot;wait until I get to the corner, then make me rage.&quot; So the idea of kuruth being used as a weapon is definitely supported by the book. It should be a weapon of last resort, but it's definitely a weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's pretty much it. I wasn't saying it wasn't a weapon, it's gauru+, but it comes with a higher potential for things you wouldn't want to happen, because werewolves don't fight in a white room. Longer gauru is nice, but you're going to be attacking every living thing you see for at least ten minutes and that's a lot of time for something to happen without you being able to retreat. Someone draws some silver weaponry and you've seriously overextended yourself.<br /> <br /> I prefer the fade to black rule, too, as it allows the Storyteller more room to move around in. Spirits can, sensing danger, hide in a zone of influence. Hosts may be destroyed, but their shards scurry off through nooks and crannies to reform later. The Claimed is dead, but did the spirit detach itself before its host died? Plus I don't want to roll for attacking everything my character sees for ten minutes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-03-2015, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T12:53:43-07:00","id":613871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=613761#post613761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer the fade to black rule, too, as it allows the Storyteller more room to move around in. Spirits can, sensing danger, hide in a zone of influence. Hosts may be destroyed, but their shards scurry off through nooks and crannies to reform later. The Claimed is dead, but did the spirit detach itself before its host died? Plus I don't want to roll for attacking everything my character sees for ten minutes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely prefer this as well. It's a huge part of the draw of Werewolf for me. And since I use that rule, Chris's point 1 isn't an issue for me because we just fade to black rather than play out the ridiculously long fight, and point 2 only gets in the way, because it removes any reason to use Kuruth against other werewolves. I would rather the temptation be there, and the players have to weigh the benefits of Death Raging against the Pure with the risks of not knowing what will happen when they come to 15 minutes later. As ST, I'm not just going to tell them &quot;there were more of the Predator Kings than there were of you, you all died while you were blacked out.&quot; I'm going to use the lost time as a way to introduce more drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T13:02:38-07:00","id":613882,"title":"","content":"So do I, but the issue with that is when not everyone in the scene is in death rage. Packmates can resist, wolfblooded players don't have the luxury, etc. Then you sort of have to play it out at least until people manage to escape or get killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T13:20:16-07:00","id":613930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=613871#post613871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I absolutely prefer this as well. It's a huge part of the draw of Werewolf for me. And since I use that rule, Chris's point 1 isn't an issue for me because we just fade to black rather than play out the ridiculously long fight</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's not just that, it's also a fight that is generally going to resolve in a tie or a loss.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and point 2 only gets in the way, because it removes any reason to use Kuruth against other werewolves. I would rather the temptation be there, and the players have to weigh the benefits of Death Raging against the Pure with the risks of not knowing what will happen when they come to 15 minutes later. As ST, I'm not just going to tell them &quot;there were more of the Predator Kings than there were of you, you all died while you were blacked out.&quot; I'm going to use the lost time as a way to introduce more drama. </div> </div> </div>I see what you mean, and I agree obviously that off-screen death is silly, but while Kuruth is a weapon, it's not always one you can control. I'm sure the Pure will have some ability to instill Kuruth in others, some are known for using silver weapons, effectively always triggering you, some of the triggers revolve around other werewolves being on your territory, and sometimes shifting to gauru is the only way to survive some wounds.<br /> <br /> But if you're going to lock-in that combat with a Pure, or even another Forsaken, the drama would be gone. You'd ignore the dog walker because you're fighting the Pure, you'd ignore the police because you're fighting the Pure. You might get arrested afterwards, if for some reason the storyteller decided to have the police wait around until you fell into hishu, but mechanically you're either going to win without agency, lose without agency, or draw with nothing happening.<br /> <br /> The temptation is there, and should be, because gauru is so much more powerful. And some player characters might even like the form, feel good or natural in it, providing the consequences don't pile up. But having it lock you into combat with another gauru is more of a drag than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-04-2015, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T14:08:46-07:00","id":614003,"title":"","content":"I've had input from Stew Wilson. Word from on high is that the intention is for everyone to be targets except your own packmates in Basu-Im. The paragraph should be corrected to:<br /> <br /> (p103) 'When in Basu-Im, a werewolf suffers rage as though in Gauru, but everyone is a victim except other *packmates* in Basu-Im. He will happily attack packmates, especially Wolf-Blooded and humans, until they join him or die. If no prey presents itself, he'll cause property damage until he can find fresh meat.'<br /> <br /> (He does quite like this emergent aspect of Basu-Im as it's being discussed here, but it's not the intended effect and isn't supported by descriptions of Basu-Im elsewhere in the text.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T14:16:03-07:00","id":614009,"title":"","content":"So now we get locked into gauru on gauru battles?<br /> <br /> I guess eating flesh will have to be the default in kuruth, since otherwise you're stuck in a loop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T14:41:41-07:00","id":614058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=614003#post614003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had input from Stew Wilson. Word from on high is that the intention is for everyone to be targets except your own packmates in Basu-Im. The paragraph should be corrected to:<br /> <br /> (p103) 'When in Basu-Im, a werewolf suffers rage as though in Gauru, but everyone is a victim except other *packmates* in Basu-Im. He will happily attack packmates, especially Wolf-Blooded and humans, until they join him or die. If no prey presents itself, he'll cause property damage until he can find fresh meat.'<br /> <br /> (He does quite like this emergent aspect of Basu-Im as it's being discussed here, but it's not the intended effect and isn't supported by descriptions of Basu-Im elsewhere in the text.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually found the bit way back in dev discussion where Stew went with the idea of death raging werewolves treating each other as being part of the same pack, so I'm surprised at this turnabout! I do have to admit to being concerned because of precisely the original issues that the rule was meant to avoid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T01:43:08-07:00","id":614717,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd encourage groups to run it whichever way they choose, as long as they're consistent. Check with your Storyteller about which one the group uses.<br /> <br /> Now I'm not saying this as a cop out - I have reasons.<br /> <br /> 1) Werewolf fiction generally falls into two camps.<br /> <br /> In the first camp, when the rampaging werewolf comes to town and the protagonist gets infected, he avoids falling into werewolf rage because of the threat it brings to those he loves, but eventually realises that the greater threat comes from the antagonist werewolf, and he surrenders to the rage knowing that he'll tear into the enemy, and it will end in the death of one of them. Often, once he's torn the throat from the antagonist, he turns on his family, who tearfully kill him to protect themselves.<br /> <br /> In the second camp, the protagonist avoids the rage because he will join the antagonist and they'll both rampage. Eventually his sorrowful family kill them both. (They might just try to kill the antagonist, hoping that it ends the curse and saves the protagonist.)<br /> <br /> I'd like to see both stories possible in WtF, depending on what the group wants. I don't want to turn either preference aside because of 'one true way'-ism, and I want to open the field for groups to explore the themes captured by both.<br /> <br /> 2) Like I said before, Stew likes the emergent aspect of this, and according to Acrozatarim, had this view in earlier development discussions. I've already asked him about adding some words to The Pack to explore this. He said no to that, because it deserves the words to explore it properly. So, what I'd propose in a future book is exploring both possible interpretations - which game themes each explores, when you'd use each one, how to play them, how they change the relationship between tribes, how they change the relationship between Pure/Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Watch this space. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T04:57:59-07:00","id":614862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=614058#post614058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've actually found the bit way back in dev discussion where Stew went with the idea of death raging werewolves treating each other as being part of the same pack, so I'm surprised at this turnabout! I do have to admit to being concerned because of precisely the original issues that the rule was meant to avoid.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why would rival predators be considered pack? Especially when they're triggering each other into a killing rage? That feels kind of strange. Maybe it was dropped because it feels a bit forced?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T10:45:57-07:00","id":615289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=613930#post613930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well it's not just that, it's also a fight that is generally going to resolve in a tie or a loss.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I see what you mean, and I agree obviously that off-screen death is silly, but while Kuruth is a weapon, it's not always one you can control. I'm sure the Pure will have some ability to instill Kuruth in others, some are known for using silver weapons, effectively always triggering you, some of the triggers revolve around other werewolves being on your territory, and sometimes shifting to gauru is the only way to survive some wounds.<br /> <br /> But if you're going to lock-in that combat with a Pure, or even another Forsaken, the drama would be gone. You'd ignore the dog walker because you're fighting the Pure, you'd ignore the police because you're fighting the Pure. You might get arrested afterwards, if for some reason the storyteller decided to have the police wait around until you fell into hishu, but mechanically you're either going to win without agency, lose without agency, or draw with nothing happening.<br /> <br /> The temptation is there, and should be, because gauru is so much more powerful. And some player characters might even like the form, feel good or natural in it, providing the consequences don't pile up. But having it lock you into combat with another gauru is more of a drag than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those just all sound like results I would not have the party wake up to. Sure, by a strict reading of the rules those are the only likely results, but the way I see it, once the characters black out, what happens during that lost time is more a matter of story than rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T10:47:40-07:00","id":615292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=612302#post612302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Yeah, but if you attacked other packmates in Death Rage TPKs would just be a thing that happened often</b></i>. As the Rahu in my group with Predator's Unmatched Pursuit and a whole host of other facets that enhance Death Rage, I know for a fact that I would kill my whole group in Death Rage, whether they matched me form for form or not. Literally they could not escape me or take me down barring Storyteller intervention. Which is cool and terrifying, I certainly don't disagree, but also might be a little too dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why, in my opinion, I think 1st Edition's Death Rage is far more terrifying than 2nd Edition's. Succumbing to Kuruth should be something to be highly avoided and never sought. Your example above is exactly why the character I played avoided Kuruth like the plague - One Kuruth and the pack would be dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T10:51:26-07:00","id":615296,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and that leads one to wonder &quot;why are werewolves not extinct again?&quot; I much prefer a setting in which every character isn't a ticking time bomb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T11:01:59-07:00","id":615314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=615296#post615296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, and that leads one to wonder &quot;why are werewolves not extinct again?&quot; I much prefer a setting in which every character isn't a ticking time bomb.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way...<br /> There are ways to avoid/minimize Kuruth, in either Edition. When it happens it should be horrifying, terrible and tragic, not only to those around the werewolf, but to the werewolf itself. It should never be an option one seeks to gain an edge (and to me, Choosing to enter <i><b>Basu-Im </b></i>is just such a tactic).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 08-04-2015, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T17:52:36-07:00","id":615835,"title":"","content":"Tough I think Kuruth have to be something to fear and avoid on most cases, to make it an recurrent source of TPK is just poor for the game.<br /> <br /> First, I don't want a game about &quot;ok, Jane went into Rage, new sheets everyone!&quot;. It isn't horror, it is silly. Have the blood of an NPC beloved by the characters, or even relevant to the game, is horrific. Maybe a Retainer or an Ally (Sanctity of Merits always in mind, tough). But not to make it easy for the kill of another PC.<br /> <br /> Second, I don't want a mechanic meant to be avoided, not used. Kuruth should be something to fear and use with caution, but also bound to happen sometimes without destroying the chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T06:01:01-07:00","id":616372,"title":"","content":"Hmmm...<br /> Interesting, since I have never actually experienced a TPK when Kuruth reared its ugly head. When Kuruth happens, those around the werewolf tend to not stick around while the Werewolf destroys things and kills people. PC's that stick around (WHY, Exactly?) while the raging wolf is doing its thing really tend to deserve what they get, in my opinion. Maybe it is a play style difference. Yes, Kuruth Happens...<br /> <br /> So, I am curious... What tends to happen at your table when Kuruth triggers and a werewolf starts killing people and destroying things? Why do you assume that it is a game ender if played up as the single most horrifying thing that can happen to you as a werewolf?<br /> <br /> 1st - You are right, if players stay around to be killed when Jane goes Kuruth, it is not the system that is Silly, it is the Player Characters. Kuruth is the embodiment of Horror. Yes, destroy NPC's that are beloved. Yes, Destroy allies or locations that are beloved. And if the PC's are bound and determined to stick it out in the same location with Jane, destroy a character or two. It is, after all, Kuruth.<br /> <br /> 2nd - Kuruth IS meant to be avoided. Says so right on the box. When you go Kuruth, people die and things get destroyed. You do not <i><b>USE </b></i>Kuruth, <i><b>KURUTH USES YOU</b></i>. And you are the poorer for it. Never have I seen a chronicle destroyed because someone went Kuruth. Does not mean that the characters should seek it out.<br /> <br /> I truly am curious about your perspective on this, because I do not really understand it. The ONE aspect of visceral horror that is endemic to Werewolf is not something that you should embrace as a lover. You can come to grips with it, you can accept that when it happens bad things follow, but you NEVER seek it out as something you CHOOSE to employ as a tactic. That way leads madness, pain and suffering.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> From my perspective in our campaign... After 500+ Karma and several years of play time, I can count the number of times one of our pack members have gone into Kuruth on one hand. Looking at that, I think it is an amazing accomplishment, to be honest, but not all that much, because as a pack, we decided that such a loss of control was bad for us, and our territory, and we took steps to minimize its occurrences. Mercy Gems are an amazing Fetish. In the end, it only enhanced our reputation. We maintain control in even the most dire of circumstances, and that makes people more than a little wary of you. Win/WIn as far as we were concerned. And yes, when it DID happen (as it will inevitably happen, no matter what precautions you take against it), for one reason or the other, it was a terrifying and horrific moment that sent ripples across the territory. It enhanced the campaign, it did not destroy it. Which is why I am not really understanding your point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 08-05-2015, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T12:37:32-07:00","id":616749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=616372#post616372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I am curious... What tends to happen at your table when Kuruth triggers and a werewolf starts killing people and destroying things? Why do you assume that it is a game ender if played up as the single most horrifying thing that can happen to you as a werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you ask this. I just started a game and in the first session we had one Basu Im and one Wasu Im (near call, but Chain Rage managed to pull him out of it).<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that your years (and mine) of experience with Death Rage are largely irrelevant, because the Domino effect is a 2nd Edition addition and dramatically improves the likeliness of multiple death rages per session. That, and the fact that the range of triggers is now much more varied due to personal triggers means that Death Rage happens in a lot of different and unpredictable ways now.<br /> <br /> Our Cahalith has the Moon set of triggers, and considering our environment and the fact that we begun the game during the Gibbous Moon, halfway through the session due to various events, he heard a howl and that was it. Wasu Im. He managed to pull himself out.<br /> <br /> But later our Ithaeur went full death rage in a crowd of distinguished politicians and other influential party guests. We had to stop her, for various common sense reasons. She killed a whole bunch of them. If my Rahu wasn't a verified badass who was stronger in Hishu than our Ithaeur even in Garou form (with the help of primal strength) we could have been in serious trouble. Anyway, I wrestled her out of the room and that was that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it was a great moment and that more or less is Kuruth behaving as it should. Inconvenient and savage, sure, but that's the game.<br /> <br /> However my concern is what would happen if my character went into Death Rage. With Primal Strength, Slaughterer and Predator's Unmatched Pursuit + the full Relentless Assault style, there is no way my going into death rage doesn't kill my packmates. Especially if there's no one around to distract my character. None of them can run fast enough to escape me, it is very likely that I will do more than their health in even if they are in Garou. (17 die attack pool in with 8-again and + 5 damage on hit). I guess that's what Wasu Im is for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 08-05-2015, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T19:28:58-07:00","id":617034,"title":"","content":"There are more than a couple of ways to avoid Basu Im, if you aren't investing in getting them I don't think you're playing wisely. It's a big enough deal that I'd want multiple people in the pack capable of getting their packmates out of Kuruth.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T18:03:37-07:00","id":618261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, since I have never actually experienced a TPK when Kuruth reared its ugly head. When Kuruth happens, those around the werewolf tend to not stick around while the Werewolf destroys things and kills people. PC's that stick around (WHY, Exactly?) while the raging wolf is doing its thing really tend to deserve what they get, in my opinion. Maybe it is a play style difference. Yes, Kuruth Happens...</div> </div> </div> </div>1st ed didn't had contagious Kuruth. Add contagious Kuruth to you not ignoring your packmates as targets and you'll have TPK happening a lot.<br /> <br /> About my point, you just took it out of context. And I don't think it should be a good thing either, much less &quot;embrace as a lover&quot;. Are you nuts!? But to use it as a dangerous resource is in keeping with the game themes. It should be a possibility, even if one full of danger.<br /> <br /> By the way, go for the descriptions of Rahu and Elodoth in 2nd ed and you'll see the game <b>clearly</b> stating that Kuruth can and should be used sparingly as a weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T19:36:17-07:00","id":618321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/608310-best-favored-form-for-a-rahu-blood-talon?p=618261#post618261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1st ed didn't had contagious Kuruth. Add contagious Kuruth to you not ignoring your packmates as targets and you'll have TPK happening a lot.<br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> By the way, go for the descriptions of Rahu and Elodoth in 2nd ed and you'll see the game <b>clearly</b> stating that Kuruth can and should be used sparingly as a weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tymaeus' point seems to be that these things are exactly why he prefers 1e Kuruth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T22:34:28-07:00","id":618541,"title":"","content":"Yes, my bad there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T08:00:14-07:00","id":618873,"title":"","content":"No worries... It just seems that people are of the opinion that Kuruth in 2nd Edition is a viable and pursuable option to use to help end fights, and to me that is just ludicrous. Apologies if I took your statements a bit out of context. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And yes, I do believe that I far prefer 1e Kuruth to 2nd Edition. Don't get me wrong here, 2nd Edition Kuruth has some interesting things about it (it is far more of a problem, though one that you can still take steps to avoid pretty efficiently), but using it to end fights is not one of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Add contagious Kuruth to you not ignoring your packmates as targets and you'll have TPK happening a lot. </div> </div> </div>Did want to comment on the above, though. I do not see it that particular way, mostly because a Werewolf in Kuruth is something that you do not stick around. If you have your Pack trying to stay with your Raging Werewolf fellow, then you are doing it wrong. Even in 2nd Edition, a Pack Mate goes Kuruth, you should not be sticking around such that you are succumbing to the contagion effect... you should be vacating the area at the fastest and most direct route available to you while he starts killing things around her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 08-07-2015, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T16:17:34-07:00","id":619543,"title":"","content":"The problem is that if they didn't ignored each other, you would risk to fall into Kuruth with him before leaving. So sometimes Kuruth would lead to at least two pack members in frenzied Rage fighting close. As soon as there are no targets nearby (almost guaranteed to happen in less than 10 minutes), they would tear each other's throats.<br /> <br /> If you want to make it more deadly, I would recommend to get rid of both the contagion and the &quot;ignore pack members also in Kuruth&quot; part.<br /> <br /> Or let it be the way it is. I personally like the idea of the entire pack in Kuruth because of one member.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}